1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,631
Orchard Core renders content items with shared templates.

2
00:00:04,631 --> 00:00:10,049
Shape alternates give one content type, or a single content item, a template of its own.

3
00:00:10,049 --> 00:00:14,257
In this video, let's name those templates, add them to a theme, and

4
00:00:14,257 --> 00:00:16,620
check which one Orchard Core picks.

5
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,897
Orchard Core builds a page from shapes.

6
00:00:23,897 --> 00:00:27,584
Each shape has a type, and a template renders that type.

7
00:00:27,584 --> 00:00:31,688
A content item on its own page usually has the type Content, so

8
00:00:31,688 --> 00:00:34,900
one Content template renders all of those items.

9
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:39,277
An alternate is another name that can render the same shape.

10
00:00:39,277 --> 00:00:43,673
Orchard Core tries the alternates first, starting with the last one added.

11
00:00:43,673 --> 00:00:47,410
If none of them has a template, it uses the shape type itself.

12
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,888
A template is named after its shape.

13
00:00:50,888 --> 00:00:55,304
In a file name, a hyphen stands for a double underscore, and a

14
00:00:55,304 --> 00:01:00,564
dot after the last hyphen adds a display type, a named way to show an item.

15
00:01:00,564 --> 00:01:05,630
So Content-Event.Summary.liquid renders the Summary display of an Event.

16
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:09,316
In a theme, templates live in the Views folder.

17
00:01:09,316 --> 00:01:13,250
A theme template wins over a module template of the same name, so

18
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:17,350
you change how a module displays content without editing the module.

19
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:26,423
For a content item, Orchard Core adds an alternate for its content type.

20
00:01:26,423 --> 00:01:31,546
A template named Content-Event applies to every Event shown on its own page,

21
00:01:31,546 --> 00:01:38,230
and Content-Event.Summary applies to events shown in the Summary display type, which lists often use.

22
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:42,661
On its own page, an item with the Autoroute part also gets an

23
00:01:42,661 --> 00:01:47,440
alternate from its path, and an item with the Alias part gets one from its alias.

24
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:51,340
In the file name, write the path with hyphens instead of slashes.

25
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:56,377
The alternate for the content type is added first, when the item is built.

26
00:01:56,377 --> 00:02:00,502
The alternates for the path and the alias are added afterwards, so they

27
00:02:00,502 --> 00:02:03,610
are tried before it, and they win for that one item.

28
00:02:07,789 --> 00:02:09,302
Here is an event page.

29
00:02:09,302 --> 00:02:13,679
The theme has no template for events, so its Content template renders them,

30
00:02:13,679 --> 00:02:15,949
and the banner holds only the title.

31
00:02:16,407 --> 00:02:20,947
The other events look the same, because they share that one Content template.

32
00:02:22,547 --> 00:02:29,393
To change every event, add a file named Content-Event.liquid to the Views folder of the theme.

33
00:02:29,393 --> 00:02:35,007
A Razor file with the same name and the extension cshtml works the same way.

34
00:02:35,757 --> 00:02:40,187
This file is based on the Content template of the theme, with two changes.

35
00:02:40,187 --> 00:02:44,617
The banner uses another image, and the word Event appears under the title.

36
00:02:46,212 --> 00:02:48,400
Open the Harvest Festival page again.

37
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,622
The banner has a different image, and the word Event appears under the title.

38
00:02:53,074 --> 00:02:55,735
The other events use the same template.

39
00:02:55,735 --> 00:03:00,289
A template named after the content type changes that type only, and the

40
00:03:00,289 --> 00:03:02,654
other content types are untouched.

41
00:03:06,854 --> 00:03:10,468
To change one event, name the file after its path.

42
00:03:10,468 --> 00:03:16,404
For the path events/night-market, the file is Content-Slug-events-night-market.liquid.

43
00:03:17,154 --> 00:03:20,814
It is based on the template of the content type, with two changes:

44
00:03:20,814 --> 00:03:24,524
a third banner image, and the words Featured event under the title.

45
00:03:26,129 --> 00:03:27,777
Open the Night Market page.

46
00:03:27,777 --> 00:03:32,269
The banner has the third image, and the words Featured event appear under the title.

47
00:03:32,730 --> 00:03:34,826
Open the Harvest Festival page again.

48
00:03:34,826 --> 00:03:38,628
It keeps the template of its content type, because only the Night Market

49
00:03:38,628 --> 00:03:40,480
has a template for its own path.

50
00:03:44,749 --> 00:03:49,422
When a template does not apply, ask Orchard Core which one rendered a shape.

51
00:03:49,422 --> 00:03:54,722
Under Settings, Debugging, the setting Write shape debug information is off by default.

52
00:03:54,722 --> 00:03:56,489
Check it and select Save.

53
00:03:56,947 --> 00:03:59,064
Then load the Night Market page.

54
00:03:59,064 --> 00:04:03,356
Its HTML source holds a pair of comments around each shape that Orchard

55
00:04:03,356 --> 00:04:08,707
Core renders for that request, and the next slide shows the pair around the Content shape.

56
00:04:10,307 --> 00:04:13,978
The first comment gives the shape type, then the template name and file

57
00:04:13,978 --> 00:04:15,980
that rendered it, with its language.

58
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:19,413
Here the name comes from the path of the item, which confirms that

59
00:04:19,413 --> 00:04:21,177
the alternate for the path won.

60
00:04:25,377 --> 00:04:28,822
A template can add an alternate when it creates a shape.

61
00:04:28,822 --> 00:04:33,267
The Liquid shape tag takes an alternate argument, the Razor tag helpers an

62
00:04:33,267 --> 00:04:38,047
alternate attribute, and a metadata element can add, remove or clear alternates.

63
00:04:38,797 --> 00:04:41,589
Add the alternate before the shape renders.

64
00:04:41,589 --> 00:04:45,635
Orchard Core picks the template first and only then runs it, so a

65
00:04:45,635 --> 00:04:48,827
template cannot change the choice made for itself.

66
00:04:49,577 --> 00:04:54,240
To add alternates for a shape type everywhere, write a shape table provider.

67
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:58,959
The Alias module describes the Content shape, and in OnDisplaying it adds the

68
00:04:58,959 --> 00:05:01,917
alias alternates to the metadata of the shape.

69
00:05:02,667 --> 00:05:06,488
A module registers its provider with AddShapeTableProvider.

70
00:05:06,488 --> 00:05:11,074
Add alternates from the least to the most specific, because the last one

71
00:05:11,074 --> 00:05:12,661
added is tried first.

72
00:05:12,661 --> 00:05:16,777
A separate video covers placement, which can add alternates too.

73
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:22,930
Alternates let a theme change the display of one content type, or one

74
00:05:22,930 --> 00:05:25,477
content item, without touching a module.

75
00:05:25,477 --> 00:05:26,917
Thanks for watching.

